---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="Send one TCP transfer over a three-hop path with an optional tunnel. Change the DF bit, ICMP filtering and MSS clamping and watch where the packet is dropped or split.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>With the defaults (no tunnel) the transfer sends <b>69</b> packets and <b>9,900</b> of 10,000 packets survive 1% fragment loss. Set <b>Tunnel overhead (bytes)</b> to <b>100</b>: the path MTU becomes <b>1,400</b>, the MSS drops to <b>1,360</b> and <b>75</b> packets are sent, with 1 extra round trip.</li>
    <li>Set <b>ICMP</b> to Blocked: the result is stalled with 0 bytes delivered. Set <b>Transfer size</b> to 1,000 bytes and it completes. Set it back to 100,000 and turn <b>MSS clamping</b> On: <b>74</b> packets, nothing wasted.</li>
    <li>Turn <b>MSS clamping</b> Off and set <b>Don't Fragment bit</b> to Cleared: the tunnel splits each packet, giving <b>138</b> wire fragments and only <b>9,801</b> of 10,000 packets surviving.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg mtu" data-mtu>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Tunnel overhead (bytes) <select class="pg-in" data-oh><option value="0" selected>0</option><option value="60">60</option><option value="100">100</option><option value="200">200</option></select></label>
      <label>Don't Fragment bit <select class="pg-in" data-df><option value="1" selected>Set</option><option value="0">Cleared</option></select></label>
      <label>ICMP <select class="pg-in" data-icmp><option value="1" selected>Allowed</option><option value="0">Blocked</option></select></label>
      <label>MSS clamping <select class="pg-in" data-clamp><option value="0" selected>Off</option><option value="1">On</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Sender MSS <select class="pg-in" data-mss><option value="1460" selected>1,460</option><option value="1360">1,360</option><option value="1200">1,200</option></select></label>
      <label>Transfer size <select class="pg-in" data-bytes><option value="1000">1,000 bytes</option><option value="100000" selected>100,000 bytes</option></select></label>
      <label>Fragment loss per 10,000 <select class="pg-in" data-loss><option value="0">0</option><option value="100" selected>100</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <h3>First full-size packet, hop by hop</h3>
    <ol class="mtu-hops" data-hops></ol>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Path MTU</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-pmtu>0</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-2)"><h3>MSS used</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-mssout>0</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-3)"><h3>Packets sent</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-packets>0</span><span class="pg-note" data-pnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-4)"><h3>Wire fragments</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-frags>0</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-5)"><h3>Packets surviving per 10,000</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-survive>0</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Result</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-result></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: three links, the middle one a tunnel with an MTU of 1,500 minus the overhead. IP and TCP headers are 20 bytes each, so a packet is MSS + 40. With DF set, a packet larger than a link is dropped, and the sender shrinks its MSS to the link limit only if ICMP is allowed (one wasted packet, one extra round trip; a real sender may lose a whole window of full-size segments). With DF cleared the router fragments, with data in multiples of 8 bytes, and losing one fragment loses the packet. MSS clamping rewrites the MSS to the smallest MTU minus 40. The tunnel overhead values are round numbers for the toy; real protocols add roughly 20 to 100 bytes (GRE 24, VXLAN 50, WireGuard 60 over IPv4).</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, numberValue, formatThousands } from '../playground';
  const HDR = 40, IP = 20, ETHERNET_MTU = 1500, FRAG_UNIT = 8, SCALE = 10000;
  function trace(path: number[], size: number, df: boolean) {
    const lines: string[] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < path.length; i++) {
      const mtu = path[i];
      if (size <= mtu) lines.push(`Hop ${i + 1}, MTU ${formatThousands(mtu)}: ${formatThousands(size)} bytes pass`);
      else if (df) { lines.push(`Hop ${i + 1}, MTU ${formatThousands(mtu)}: ${formatThousands(size)} bytes with DF set, dropped`); break; }
      else {
        const per = Math.floor((mtu - IP) / FRAG_UNIT) * FRAG_UNIT;
        lines.push(`Hop ${i + 1}, MTU ${formatThousands(mtu)}: fragmented into ${Math.ceil((size - IP) / per)} pieces of at most ${formatThousands(per)} data bytes`);
        size = per + IP;
      }
    }
    return lines;
  }
  function transfer(path: number[], mss0: number, bytes: number, df: boolean, icmp: boolean, clamp: boolean, loss: number) {
    const pmtu = Math.min(...path);
    let mss = clamp ? Math.min(mss0, pmtu - HDR) : mss0;
    const size = Math.min(mss, bytes) + HDR;
    let packets: number, frags = 1, wasted = 0, result: string, ok = true;
    if (size <= pmtu) { packets = Math.ceil(bytes / mss); result = 'complete'; }
    else if (!df) { frags = Math.ceil((mss + IP) / (Math.floor((pmtu - IP) / FRAG_UNIT) * FRAG_UNIT)); packets = Math.ceil(bytes / mss); result = 'complete (fragmented)'; }
    else if (icmp) { mss = pmtu - HDR; packets = Math.ceil(bytes / mss); wasted = 1; result = 'complete after PMTUD'; }
    else { packets = 0; result = 'stalled, 0 bytes delivered'; ok = false; }
    let survive = SCALE;
    for (let k = 0; k < frags; k++) survive = Math.floor(survive * (SCALE - loss) / SCALE);
    return { pmtu, mss, packets: packets + wasted, frags: packets * frags, wasted, result, survive, ok, size };
  }

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-mtu]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root); const val = numberValue(q);
    const setText = (s: string, v: string) => { q(s).textContent = v; };
    function draw() {
      const path = [ETHERNET_MTU, ETHERNET_MTU - val('[data-oh]'), ETHERNET_MTU];
      const df = val('[data-df]') === 1, icmp = val('[data-icmp]') === 1, clamp = val('[data-clamp]') === 1;
      const mss0 = val('[data-mss]'), bytes = val('[data-bytes]'), loss = val('[data-loss]');
      const r = transfer(path, mss0, bytes, df, icmp, clamp, loss);
      const hops = q('[data-hops]'); hops.textContent = '';
      const first = (clamp ? Math.min(mss0, r.pmtu - HDR) : mss0) + HDR;
      for (const l of trace(path, Math.min(first, bytes + HDR), df)) { const li = document.createElement('li'); li.textContent = l; hops.appendChild(li); }
      setText('[data-pmtu]', formatThousands(r.pmtu)); setText('[data-mssout]', formatThousands(r.mss));
      setText('[data-packets]', formatThousands(r.packets)); setText('[data-pnote]', r.wasted ? '1 wasted, 1 extra round trip' : '');
      setText('[data-frags]', formatThousands(r.frags)); setText('[data-survive]', r.ok ? `${formatThousands(r.survive)} of ${formatThousands(SCALE)}` : 'none');
      setText('[data-result]', r.result);
      setText('[data-verdict]', !r.ok ? 'Black hole: the oversized packet is dropped, the ICMP message that would explain it is filtered, and the sender retries the same size forever. Small requests still work.'
        : r.result === 'complete (fragmented)' ? 'It works, but every packet becomes several fragments, and losing any one loses the packet.'
        : r.wasted ? 'Path MTU discovery worked: one packet was wasted and the MSS dropped to the link limit.'
        : r.pmtu < ETHERNET_MTU ? 'The segments already fit the tunnel, so nothing was dropped.' : 'Every link carries the full-size packet.');
    }
    root.querySelectorAll('select').forEach((el) => el.addEventListener('input', draw));
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .mtu .mtu-hops { margin: 8px 0 12px 1.2em; padding: 0; }
  .playground .mtu .mtu-hops li { margin: 2px 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
